ser":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T16:28:14-07:00","id":1309322,"title":"","content":"How do the Hedge Denizen and Goblin Queen Conditions apply to non-changelings with regard to fae traits like Wyrd and Glamour? Also, what happens when a mortal child taken to replace a Goblin Queen comes of age?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1307874-upcoming-changeling-the-lost-interview-with-developer-meghan-fitzgerald?p=1309304#post1309304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is extra important question because True Fae can create Eidolons in the Hedge and I'm not sure how to treat that mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>treat other characters as</i> important eidolons \u2014 which is a mechanically defined term in the oneiromancy system \u2014 for the purposes of using oneiromancy in places that aren't Bastions and their contents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T16:51:30-07:00","id":1309325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1307874-upcoming-changeling-the-lost-interview-with-developer-meghan-fitzgerald?p=1309321#post1309321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">will these questions posted here have to be reposted into the interview questions? (first time doing this)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, it's an audio interview. I'll collect the questions, talk to Meghan, and post a link to the interview on this thread. If you want to check out any of our past interviews, you can check out our past interviews and other episodes here: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T19:33:23-07:00","id":1309355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElfSpeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1307874-upcoming-changeling-the-lost-interview-with-developer-meghan-fitzgerald?p=1309325#post1309325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, it's an audio interview. I'll collect the questions, talk to Meghan, and post a link to the interview on this thread. If you want to check out any of our past interviews, you can check out our past interviews and other episodes here: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>thank you very much kind sir","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T02:35:38-07:00","id":1309396,"title":"","content":"This is a bit of an odd question, but are there any plans for introducing another Seeming to second edition?<br /> <br /> I appreciate that we technically have Grimms from Dark Eras, but they don\u2019t quite fit second edition as is, and I have seen that no (open) plans to bring them up to code as it were. I mostly ask due to supplements adding new options of that kind in other gamelines, such as Demon (Analysts) and Beast (Inguma and Talassii) and curiosity springs eternal. Granted, Changeling is quite broad in its options for Seemings and Kiths to begin with, even compared to other gamelines, so I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if this was a \u201cNo\u201d.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another question. Are there True Fae who are \u201cgood\u201d - that is, ones whose actions and domains are such that their Changelings genuinely don\u2019t want to leave, and thus why nobody hears of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 05-02-2019, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T04:36:43-07:00","id":1309614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElfSpeaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1307874-upcoming-changeling-the-lost-interview-with-developer-meghan-fitzgerald?p=1309311#post1309311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes I will.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T04:38:08-07:00","id":1309615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1307874-upcoming-changeling-the-lost-interview-with-developer-meghan-fitzgerald?p=1309396#post1309396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit of an odd question, but are there any plans for introducing another Seeming to second edition?<br /> <br /> I appreciate that we technically have Grimms from Dark Eras, but they don\u2019t quite fit second edition as is, and I have seen that no (open) plans to bring them up to code as it were. I mostly ask due to supplements adding new options of that kind in other gamelines, such as Demon (Analysts) and Beast (Inguma and Talassii) and curiosity springs eternal. Granted, Changeling is quite broad in its options for Seemings and Kiths to begin with, even compared to other gamelines, so I wouldn\u2019t be surprised if this was a \u201cNo\u201d.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another question. Are there True Fae who are \u201cgood\u201d - that is, ones whose actions and domains are such that their Changelings genuinely don\u2019t want to leave, and thus why nobody hears of them?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think I heard somewhere that nice True Fae is likely a sign of contagion, but I don't remember where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T09:18:36-07:00","id":1309665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1307874-upcoming-changeling-the-lost-interview-with-developer-meghan-fitzgerald?p=1309396#post1309396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Another question. Are there True Fae who are \u201cgood\u201d - that is, ones whose actions and domains are such that their Changelings genuinely don\u2019t want to leave, and thus why nobody hears of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you're a &quot;Good True Fae&quot; you probably don't go around taking people in the first place? And If they don't really have emissaries, then why would you hear about them?<br /> <br /> The Lost Style Guide does clarify that there's a difference between Strangers and those who are Keepers based on the practice, so who knows? But real or not, it's not really the purview of Lost to explore things that don't really interact with their reality, so such entities are moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T09:47:21-07:00","id":1309666,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your input. I'm going to close the interview to new questions at this point since I'll be talking to Meghan in a couple of hours. The interview itself will be aired either June 3 or June 17 depending on the editing time. I'll post it here when it's available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:31:29-07:00","id":1309680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1307874-upcoming-changeling-the-lost-interview-with-developer-meghan-fitzgerald?p=1309665#post1309665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you're a &amp;quot;Good True Fae&amp;quot; you probably don't go around taking people in the first place? And If they don't really have emissaries, then why would you hear about them?<br /> <br /> The Lost Style Guide does clarify that there's a difference between Strangers and those who are Keepers based on the practice, so who knows? But real or not, it's not really the purview of Lost to explore things that don't really interact with their reality, so such entities are moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I am part of a Discord server where at least two people have stated my question word for word - that there are good ones, you just don\u2019t hear about them. While I don\u2019t believe there are, or at least they are too alien to fit our definition of nice/good, I wanted to make sure that I wasn\u2019t perpetuating another myth like Changelings all becoming Gentry at Wyrd 10 Clarity 0, or Changeling Arcadia being the same as Mage Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:35:51-07:00","id":1309683,"title":"","content":"I mean, you would expect at least some of these gentry interact with keepers, so I see the argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T10:36:20-07:00","id":1309684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1307874-upcoming-changeling-the-lost-interview-with-developer-meghan-fitzgerald?p=1309680#post1309680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps, but I am part of a Discord server where at least two people have stated my question word for word - that there are good ones, you just don\u2019t hear about them. While I don\u2019t believe there are, or at least they are too alien to fit our definition of nice/good, I wanted to make sure that I wasn\u2019t perpetuating another myth like Changelings all becoming Gentry at Wyrd 10 Clarity 0, or Changeling Arcadia being the same as Mage Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T09:04:52-07:00","id":1319300,"title":"","content":"We have posted the interview and you can find it here: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/episode-29-meghan-fitzgerald-interview\" target=\"_blank\">http://thestorytold.libsyn.com/episo...rald-interview</a><br /> <br /> I hope you enjoy it. As with previous interviews, we don't have a text version, but if someone would like to create one, I'm happy to share the outline with the questions (though we do deviate somewhat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T11:59:09-07:00","id":1319550,"title":"","content":"Very happy with how the interview went, and how the questions were presented. The answer to my question of \u201cAre there \u2018Good\u2019 True Fae whose realms people don\u2019t want to leave and thus people don\u2019t hear about them\u201d was very well put, putting a nuanced look on how the Gentry and their servants operate. Thanks to Meghan and ElfSpeaker for this~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T12:30:57-07:00","id":1319556,"title":"","content":"I'm glad to hear you liked it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-21T03:43:28-07:00","id":1319898,"title":"","content":"Thanks for asking about the Toronto Freehold, disappointing answer, but you did me a solid. <br /> <br /> It's interesting that Kith and Kin is more Tier 1 with not just Kiths, but Regalia, Contracts, and Motley stuff, while the Companion is more Tier two, with Courts, qausi Court like Organizations, Tokens with Oaths, Entitlements, and stuff like that. <br /> <br /> Listening to her talk made me wonder if one can be a member of multiple freeholds or international Motley's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}